## 15. Deferred decisions and dependency queue

**Resolve in Gate 1 tests/research:** Camera selection and movement restrictions; exact photo-grade formula and feedback; initial monster cue/provocation; map variation approach; acceptable trail pacing, target round duration, and evidence carrying count; what minimum subject framing means across devices; formal test thresholds.

**Gate 2 decisions:** Party/queue UX for 1–4, recoverable physical evidence representation, death timing and rescue edge cases, incentive size/anti-farming, journal persistence and migrations, contract generation, individual extraction/spectating, reconnect/disconnect, multiplayer anti-exploit.

**Gate 3 decisions:** Final cryptid roster and model selection, aesthetic fidelity, soundtrack/audio/VFX, accessibility, controller support, polished lobby, high-quality onboarding, progression depth, earned cosmetic inventory, economy sinks and sources, and purchase flow design.

**Deferred commercial decisions:** Robux prices, currency packs, boosters, luck modifiers, paid party expansion, passes, bundles, cosmetics catalogue, offer timing, purchase protection, randomized products, and marketing spend. Avoid pay-to-win dynamics; assess demand and platform policies before selecting products.

**Separate product research:** Authentic captured screenshot retention, gallery privacy/moderation/storage and sharing; whether a phone-screen ViewportFrame is worth its complexity; new habitats; procedural map generation; rare encounter event depth.

## 16. Next deliverable and authorization checklist

**This document completes the requested design brief, not the prototype.** A future **read-only Rg1 readiness audit** could verify repository state and propose a small Gate 1 implementation plan. Even that audit requires a separate request before taking action outside this conversation.

Before authorizing any build, explicitly agree on: (1) which repository/worktree is targeted, (2) whether Claude may modify files, (3) whether Studio changes are allowed, (4) scope confined to Gate 1, (5) test and rollback procedure, (6) allowed use of third-party assets after license verification, and (7) required completion report.

**Final status:** Design specification complete; camera architecture not approved; no repository changes; no Google Doc edits; no asset generation; no implementation authorization.
